`services/llm.py::complete()` takes `tools` and `tool_choice`, and `LLMResponse` carries the tool calls a model asked for (Phase 4B section 8). Rules L1 to L8 are untouched: a call that asked for tools writes one usage record and is priced exactly like one that did not. Both self-hosted provider types now also require a remote URL on their external integration, checked at save time and again at call time - litellm's fallback for `openai/` is `api.openai.com`, which would send this deployment's key and its event payload to a third party, and its fallback for `ollama/` is a loopback address that means nothing inside a container.
